See README.md in this directory for the current story: this directory holds
`catalog.json`, the machine-readable index of every real, individually
reviewed Hunspell dictionary smaragd can download on request, and
`placeholders/`, the tiny bundled fallbacks below. The actual per-language
dictionary files (`<language_code>/`, each with its own `LICENSE` and
`SOURCE`) live in a separate repo,
https://github.com/ljantzen/smaragd-dictionaries, not here — see that repo's
own NOTICE for why redistributing them there, as genuinely separate files, is
fine even where one (`nb_NO`, GPL-2.0-only) would be a real problem if it
were ever combined or linked into smaragd's own binary.

`placeholders/en_US.aff`/`.dic` and `placeholders/nb_NO.aff`/`.dic` are a
different thing entirely: tiny (~20-word), hand-written word lists with no
licensing question of their own, `include_bytes!`-bundled directly into the
compiled binary so English/Norwegian have *something* working immediately,
before either real dictionary has been downloaded. Every other language does
nothing at all (flags no words) until its real dictionary is downloaded — see
`src/spellcheck.rs`'s module doc comment for the full explanation of why.
